{"id":3504,"date":"2021-08-08T08:39:26","date_gmt":"2021-08-08T15:39:26","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3504"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:35:45","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:35:45","slug":"0-3-pycharm-edu-orientation","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-3-pycharm-edu-orientation\/","title":{"rendered":"0.5: Pycharm Edu Orientation"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221430efe3e\" name=\"6a221430efe3e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Checklist<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This lesson will go over the following steps:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Create a the CoDrone Mini Project Directory<\/li>\n<li>Install the CoDrone Mini Package<\/li>\n<li>Run your first test flight<\/li>\n<li>Open and use the Python Console<\/li>\n<li>Label your micro USB cable<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>If you have any trouble completing these steps throughout the lesson, please reach out to us on the <a href=\"https:\/\/forum.robolink.com\/\">forum<\/a> so that we can help you get started![\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221430f00e1\" name=\"6a221430f00e1\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Set up PyCharm Edu<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To use CoDrone Mini with PyCharm, you will need to open a new project with the right environment and install the CoDrone Mini library. Follow the video below to get started.<\/p>\n<div style=\"width: 1200px;\" class=\"wp-video\"><video class=\"wp-video-shortcode\" id=\"video-3504-1\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" preload=\"metadata\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"video\/mp4\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Install-Codrone-mini-package.mp4?_=1\" \/><a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Install-Codrone-mini-package.mp4\">https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Install-Codrone-mini-package.mp4<\/a><\/video><\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221430f0224\" name=\"6a221430f0224\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Test Program<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To make sure you have everything installed, let&#8217;s run a test program. First, connect your controller to your controller and power on your CoDrone Mini.[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]To keep our files organized, we are going to create directories for each of the islands (lessons) that we will progress through. To do this and do your first flight test, watch the video below:<\/p>\n<div style=\"width: 1200px;\" class=\"wp-video\"><video class=\"wp-video-shortcode\" id=\"video-3504-2\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" preload=\"metadata\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"video\/mp4\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Directories.mp4?_=2\" \/><a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Directories.mp4\">https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Directories.mp4<\/a><\/video><\/div>\n<p>Now you are going to run a simple test code that will make your drone take off, hover, and land. Copy and paste the following code into a new file and run the program. Make sure you have enough space! If you have trouble pairing, move on to the next step.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\ndrone.takeoff()\r\ndrone.hover(3)\r\ndrone.land()<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221430f02f3\" name=\"6a221430f02f3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The Python Console<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Now that we know how to create and run python programs in Pycharm, we need to look at another useful tool called the Python Console. Watch the video below and follow along to learn more about this:<\/p>\n<div style=\"width: 1200px;\" class=\"wp-video\"><video class=\"wp-video-shortcode\" id=\"video-3504-3\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" preload=\"metadata\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"video\/mp4\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Python-Console.mp4?_=3\" \/><a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Python-Console.mp4\">https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/08\/Getting-Started-Python-Console.mp4<\/a><\/video><\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221430f036f\" name=\"6a221430f036f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Driver Installation<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you were able to pair successfully in the last step, you can skip the driver installation. Some devices will not recognize the CoDrone Mini controller so you will need to download a driver. You can download the driver below for your device:<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1a2NPQoyjvr8hwWxO1I5T-ZFowznYsx9E\/view\">Download MacOS Driver<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1ge1JZaClAL1ERtx7ATJFxvAFaHGX8VBM\/view\">Download Windows Driver<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/github.com\/juliagoda\/CH341SER\">Download Linux Driver<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION:<\/strong> The drivers for CoDrone Mini and CoDrone Lite\/Pro are <strong>different<\/strong>. Make sure you install from the links above if you are using CoDrone Mini.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221430f03e0\" name=\"6a221430f03e0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Label your microUSB cable<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Mark the USB cable that came in the package with a tape\u2014choose something obvious, like a colorful tape. This is because some USB cables only provide power but don\u2019t transfer data, so you\u2019ll want to distinguish it from others.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2434&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221430f0437\" name=\"6a221430f0437\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>All done!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You are ready to start learning Python with CoDrone Mini! Click the next lesson to get started. Please leave any feedback or issues you had by emailing us at support@robolink.com. When you email us, let us know you are contacting us about the Python CoDrone Mini setup process and be detailed with your issue.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 Checklist [vc_column_text]This lesson will go over the following steps: Create a the CoDrone Mini Project Directory Install the CoDrone Mini Package Run your first test flight Open&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-3-pycharm-edu-orientation\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":2426,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3473,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2125,2177,2134],"class_list":["post-3504","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-python","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3504","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":6,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3504\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":8680,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3504\/revisions\/8680"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2426"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3504"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=3504"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=3504"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}